// }
// large_xml += "</students>";
// Pass this `large_xml` string as the first argument to `get_student_info`.
```
Executing the program with such a large XML string will cause `xmlReadMemory` to allocate a substantial amount of memory, potentially leading to an out-of-memory error or significant performance degradation, thus causing a Denial of Service.

THE CODE IS SAFE, with the exception of the identified DoS vulnerability due to unchecked XML input size.

